## Delegation Commands

### Per Scope Contract Execution

**SC1 — Golden Path:**
```
/implement "Create tests/e2e/product-detail/golden-path.spec.ts implementing complete customer journey test for product sennheiser-hd-800-s. Test must: (1) navigate to product page, (2) verify product name in h1, (3) verify price visible, (4) verify main image has src, (5) click breadcrumb Home and verify navigation to /, (6) go back and click breadcrumb Products and verify /products/headphones, (7) go back and increase quantity to 2, (8) add to cart and verify cart count, (9) click first related product and verify successful navigation (no 404). Use data-testid attributes for selectors. Target 8 browser configurations per playwright.config.ts."
```

**SC2 — RWD Stress:**
```
/implement "Create tests/e2e/product-detail/rwd.spec.ts with viewport matrix testing 5 breakpoints: 390×844, 844×390, 768×1024, 1280×720, 1440×900. Each test must: (1) set viewport, (2) navigate to product, (3) assert no horizontal overflow (body.width <= viewport.width + 1), (4) assert h1 visible, (5) mobile: verify stacked layout (image Y < info Y), verify all buttons >= 44px, (6) desktop: verify side-by-side layout (image Y ≈ info Y within 100px). Use boundingBox() for layout assertions."
```

**SC3 — Edge Cases:**
```
/implement "Create tests/e2e/product-detail/edge-cases.spec.ts with 4 test cases: (1) invalid slug /products/non-existent-12345 → expect 404 or 'Product Not Found' text, (2) product with no images → expect data-testid='image-gallery-placeholder' visible, (3) out of stock product → expect button disabled with 'Out of Stock' text, (4) zoom modal keyboard: open zoom, press Escape, expect modal closed. Use real test products or mocks."
```

**SC4 — Integration:**
```
/implement "Create tests/integration/product-api.spec.ts with 2 test cases: (1) getProductBySlug('sennheiser-hd-800-s') returns object matching { _id: string, name: string, displayPrice: number, stock: number, sku: string, slug: { current: string }, catalogueLocationKeys: array }, (2) getRelatedProducts returns array where each item has slug.current matching /^[a-z0-9-]+$/. Use real Sanity client calls (not mocks)."
```

**SC5 — Infrastructure:**
```
/implement "Add data-testid attributes for test targeting: (1) verify ImageGallery has data-testid='main-image' or 'image-gallery', (2) add data-testid='related-products' to RelatedProducts section, (3) create tests/utils/product-detail-helpers.ts with shared selectors and retry patterns. NO styling changes, only data-testid additions."
```

